kgf 0.6
language: python-strict
sources: .pyx
extends: python

# A project-local dialect of Python.
#
# The build step in this project compiles `.pyx` sources with the same syntax
# as the `.py` files beside them, so the only thing this overlay has to say
# is which extension carries it: `extends: python` inherits the lexer, the
# grammar, the semantics and the resolver wholesale, and `sources:` is the
# one section inheritance deliberately never copies.
#
# This is the shape a project-local overlay is meant to take — a few lines
# naming a difference, not a fork of the base spec.
